WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:03.120
- I believe that the Yale
School of Public Health

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.460
has the chance to define public health,

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.220
scholarship, education, and practice

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:09.780
for the next century,

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.210
to define who's part of public health,

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:15.870
how we do it, how we identify
and address health problems

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:19.290
in an inclusive, equitable,
and impactful way.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:20.610
The ultimate objective

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.950
for the Yale School of Public Health

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:26.520
is for us to be recognized
globally as the school

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:29.613
that is transforming the
future of human health.

00:00:30.978 --> 00:00:34.395
(gentle symphonic music)

00:00:40.141 --> 00:00:42.900
I see there being four pillars

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.030
of a school of public health

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:48.180
that defines the future of our field.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.070
Those are inclusivity.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.070
It is, of course, core to
the field of public health,

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.410
but it's also how we are going to succeed

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.420
as we move forward.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:01.380
Inclusivity is about having a
diverse, equitable, inclusive,

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:05.190
and belonging-focused
environment within our school

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.410
for faculty, staff, and students.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.720
But it's also about being inclusive

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:13.410
of community voices, of lived experience,

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.720
of folks who we may not
traditionally think of

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.750
as being part of public health at all.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:20.940
Innovation and entrepreneurship,

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:23.040
making sure that we're set up to make sure

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.800
that public health innovations

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:29.070
can thrive in either for-profit

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:31.470
or not-for-profit environments.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:34.500
The third pillar is around communication.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.570
As we learned all too well during COVID,

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:39.990
it's essential for all
of us, students, faculty,

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.250
and the world at large

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:44.430
to know how to communicate
about public health

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.920
and scientific knowledge.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.960
The last pillar that is essential for us

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:49.860
as we move forward

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:52.080
into the public health
school of the future

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.810
is around data-driven leadership.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:59.010
That's the ability for us to
use our disciplinary skills

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:02.250
to identify problems, gather data sets,

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:04.200
to look at the details,

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.900
and then figure out what to do next.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.370
Public health is only as good

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:11.130
as the action that we
take at the other side,

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.330
the impact that we have

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:14.640
on the health of our local community,

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.890
as well as the nation and the globe,

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:20.250
those are the skills that we
have to impart in our students,

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:23.790
but also that we as faculty
and staff and alumni,

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.173
need to be dedicated to.

00:02:26.215 --> 00:02:29.820
(gentle symphonic music)

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:33.300
C.E.A Winslow founded our
School of Public Health

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.370
108 years ago,

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:38.040
based on the idea that
core to public health

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:39.570
is the community,

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.940
and also core to public health

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:45.390
is empowering the community for change.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:46.800
That's one of the philosophies

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:50.610
that informs my leadership
style in general,

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:53.130
informs my decision to assume the deanship

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:55.470
here at the Yale School of Public Health,

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:57.900
and that is core to our function

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.060
as a school of public health,

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:04.230
but going forwards, it is
incumbent on us to do more.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.060
Public health only succeeds

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.850
when we have the public at its core,

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:12.120
when we listen to, partner with,

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.520
and sometimes are led by

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.953
the needs of the communities
in which we work.

00:03:18.085 --> 00:03:21.870
(gentle symphonic music)

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:23.250
As an emergency physician,

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:26.790
I know that I'm only as good
as the team that I work with,

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:28.290
and so my commitment as a leader

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.600
is to making sure that everyone on my team

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:34.020
is set up for success,
knows what their role is,

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.050
and is empowered to do
everything that they can

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.103
for the greater good.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:42.397
(gentle symphonic music)

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:48.000
Oh, here at Yale, we
have tremendous potential

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.490
to influence and make progress

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:52.800
on firearm injury prevention,

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.870
both within the School of Public Health,

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:58.980
but also in partnership with
other schools across Yale.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:01.290
We have a number of brilliant researchers

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:02.970
at the Yale School of Public Health

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.130
who are already thinking about

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:07.740
many of those baseline risk factors

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:10.620
for firearm injury and how to modify them.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:13.980
We have a tremendous
opportunity to set the standard,

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.350
not just as an academic community,

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:19.500
but as a city, and as a state,

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.960
that can help lead the rest of the nation.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.940
Thank you, from the bottom of my heart

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:27.843
for your commitment to the
Yale School of Public Health.

